Short:        DICE Compiler Documentation (HTML)
Author:       Matthew J Fletcher (DICE Development Group)
Uploader:     amimjf hotmail com (Matthew J Fletcher)
Type:         dev/c
Version:      0.4
Replaces:     -
Requires:     -
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Distribution: Aminet

This archive contains the full documentation set for the now freeware
DICE compiler. This version is just a quick conversion from the better
AmigaGuide, 'dice-docs-3.xx.lha', which i would recomend. However if
you are using DICE on a X-BSD box then this is for you.

The DICE Development Group is Headed by Richard Drummond (of CU Amiga &
Amiga Format Fame) he posted a re-compiled and rebuilt version of Matt
Dillions source relase of version 3.15 of dice on 02/10/98, i was at the
time looking for a new compiler, having used freedice for some time i
decided to get this new version (3.16).

http://www.drummond.u-net.com - Richards Web Page (Full Download)

http://www.onelist.com/archives.cgi/dice - DICE Mailing List (its free !!)

http://bounce.to/matts/index13.html - my DICE section

